{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5206-1","published":"2026-11-11T12:57:10Z","modified":"2026-11-12T12:15:06.258257552Z","related":["CVE-2026-35189","CVE-2026-54872","CVE-2026-75806","CVE-2026-77696","CVE-2026-84782"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-35189","CVE-2026-54872","CVE-2026-75806","CVE-2026-77696","CVE-2026-84782"],"summary":"Security update for openssl-1_1","details":"This update for openssl-1_1 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-35189: Excessive Memory Allocation in Relative CRLDP Processing (bsc#1280589).\n- CVE-2026-54872: Timing Side-Channel in Scalar Multiplication for Non-NIST EC Curves (bsc#1280591).\n- CVE-2026-75806: Unauthenticated and Undersized DTLS 1.2 AEAD Record Causes DoS (bsc#1280597).\n- CVE-2026-77696: Timing Side-Channel in SM2 Signature Generation (bsc#1280598).\n- CVE-2026-84782: DTLS Retransmits Handshake Messages From a Stale Buffer Offset (bsc#1280587).\n\nThis update for openssl-1_1 fixes the following issue:\n\n- Add -flive-patching=inline-clone to avoid untraceable inter-procedural\n  optimizations (bsc#1277247).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openssl-1_1","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP6-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/openssl-1_1&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2015%20SP6-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libopenssl-1_1-devel":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1","libopenssl1_1":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1","libopenssl1_1-32bit":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1","openssl-1_1":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5206-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssl-1_1","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server for SAP Applications 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/openssl-1_1&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%20for%20SAP%20Applications%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.1.1w-150600.5.43.1"}]}],"ecosyste